  `phantom_f7_class`.  Therefore F7 should mean a concrete residual basis
  vector outside the current certificate image, not an anonymous hard row.

[3] Two proof angles extracted
  angle A: observability-first residual proof
    Work fiberwise.  The route leak after coarse ET+unit is killed by the
    first separating sidecar: arc topology for 13 fibers, safe-component
    stalk for the remaining 2.  Later primitive decks and magnitude data
    are fallback certificates, not replacements for the local tooth order.
  angle B: cycle-generation / Hodge-style proof
    Treat every residual cochain as a row in Cert(P)->H_res(P).  Partial
    cubes, simplex faces, rectangle residues, endpoint owners, Ramanujan
    periods, Haar squares, and state-lifts are columns.  The proof closes
    only when each row is generated, dual-annihilated, descended, boundary-
    stopped, or emitted as an explicit F7/THM-572 class.

